# Merge quality gate (mandatory)

**Never merge a PR to `main` if any required check is red or pending.**

## Before every merge

Run on the PR branch:

```bash
gh pr checks <number>
```

Do not merge until **all** of the following are `pass` (or `skipping` when expected):

| Check | When required |
|---|---|
| **SonarCloud Code Analysis** | Always — any PR touching `app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, `scripts/` |
| **Lint and build** | Web paths changed (see `web-quality.yml`) |
| **Build debug APK** | Android paths changed (see `android-native.yml`) |

If SonarCloud shows `fail`, **stop**. Fix the Sonar issues on the branch, push, wait for green, then merge. Do not bypass.

## Why

PR #121 was merged with Sonar red (`Math.random()` in `lib/boss-api-handlers.js`), breaking the main quality gate. That must not happen again.

## GitHub branch protection (human setup)

An agent cannot configure this. Owner must add these as **required status checks** on `main` in GitHub → Settings → Branches:

- `SonarCloud Code Analysis`
- `Lint and build`
- `Build debug APK` (when Android CI applies)

Until branch protection is enabled, agents must self-enforce via `gh pr checks`.
